WEBVTT

00:09.926 --> 00:11.458
You again...?

00:11.883 --> 00:13.507
Don't blame him.

00:13.981 --> 00:15.513
This one's my fault.

00:23.390 --> 00:26.584
And why are there so many people here?

00:27.760 --> 00:31.021
Apparently Ume called them in
after I contacted him.

00:31.575 --> 00:32.775
Anyway, take a seat.

00:33.433 --> 00:35.821
Ugh, fine.

00:36.221 --> 00:39.125
Wait, Sakura, is that it?!

00:39.126 --> 00:40.960
Huh? What do you mean?

00:41.409 --> 00:43.563
I-I mean...

00:45.526 --> 00:50.406
A-All the devas and their aides
are here, which means...

00:51.076 --> 00:55.353
what happened yesterday was just that big a deal.

00:57.760 --> 01:00.061
Ah! You're all here already?!

01:02.504 --> 01:06.307
Dammit, man, you need to learn
to act like a real Primo!

01:06.424 --> 01:08.909
That's unusual. Typically he's here first.

01:08.910 --> 01:10.652
Guess these things happen!

01:10.898 --> 01:14.006
Good morning, Ume! It's totally fine!

01:14.424 --> 01:15.876
Think he overslept?

01:16.313 --> 01:20.283
Sakura, Suo, Nirei. Thanks for coming so early.

01:21.667 --> 01:22.338
Now...

01:26.000 --> 01:27.310
Let's get started!

03:01.035 --> 03:04.038
[East Wind Shopping Street]

03:20.138 --> 03:23.599
[Bofurin]

03:24.172 --> 03:26.461
Kotoha's specialty sandwiches!

03:26.843 --> 03:29.883
It's early, so I figured we
could eat while we talk!

03:30.215 --> 03:31.272
I got coffee, too.

03:31.273 --> 03:33.685
Nice! I'mma grab an egg sandwich!

03:33.686 --> 03:34.658
Coffee, please.

03:34.812 --> 03:36.363
So this is why you were late.

03:36.972 --> 03:38.103
In that case...

03:38.104 --> 03:41.469
Wow, you're so nice, Ume!
Killing us with kindness!

03:41.470 --> 03:44.492
Lucky me! I skimped on breakfast.

03:45.421 --> 03:47.526
Hey, what the hell is this?

03:47.704 --> 03:50.283
Hmm... A picnic, I suppose?

03:51.310 --> 03:52.166
Thanks.

03:56.707 --> 03:57.310
Here.

03:57.920 --> 03:59.520
I made plenty.

03:59.852 --> 04:01.520
Thank ya, Kotoha!

04:01.969 --> 04:04.572
You make the best sandwiches in all of Japan!

04:05.175 --> 04:07.378
Enough. Take them and get going.

04:08.283 --> 04:10.160
This meeting's important, isn't it?

04:10.664 --> 04:11.796
You're gonna be late.

04:15.981 --> 04:17.175
Ah, thanks.

04:18.363 --> 04:19.680
Oh, thank you.

04:20.123 --> 04:22.578
Ooh, thanks, Sugishita!

04:22.707 --> 04:25.267
And even after you helped me carry it all here!

04:25.870 --> 04:27.482
No, it's nothing.

04:27.483 --> 04:29.396
S-Sugishita!

04:30.880 --> 04:32.043
I'll take over!

04:32.135 --> 04:33.526
Good morning, Sugishita.

04:39.901 --> 04:40.909
Sorry!

04:40.910 --> 04:43.421
That face screams, "What are you doing here?"

04:44.560 --> 04:46.904
Thuh... Thank you.

04:48.030 --> 04:49.476
- Watch it, dumbass!
- Thanks!

04:50.246 --> 04:51.495
Seriously...

04:54.492 --> 04:56.889
You bastard! Give me one, too!

04:56.890 --> 04:58.750
- Sakura, you can have this one!
- Where's mine?!

04:59.181 --> 05:01.280
You have more cups!

05:09.833 --> 05:11.525
You! Me! Outside!

05:11.526 --> 05:13.894
The hell am I supposed to drink from this?!

05:13.895 --> 05:15.710
You really don't get along!

05:15.926 --> 05:19.033
Hiragi let slip that their first day was rough.

05:19.304 --> 05:22.535
Huh. These firsties sure are spirited.

05:22.910 --> 05:26.344
Come on, Sugishita. Don't be so mean.

05:26.701 --> 05:28.455
You can't waste cups like that.

05:33.433 --> 05:35.015
H-He fixed it.

05:35.218 --> 05:37.132
Though it looks ready to fall over.

05:40.258 --> 05:43.206
Well done! You didn't waste the cup.

05:43.440 --> 05:44.123
That's it?

05:44.209 --> 05:46.529
Way to go, Ume. So forgiving.

05:46.713 --> 05:47.944
How is this okay?!

05:53.076 --> 05:55.600
You bastard! Let's take this outside!

05:56.166 --> 05:58.116
Enough already, you two!

05:59.784 --> 06:03.390
Umemiya, I appreciate the food,
but let's get into this already.

06:05.249 --> 06:06.498
Oh, right, right.

06:07.040 --> 06:09.015
Now, let's see, first off...

06:09.920 --> 06:12.215
You want an explanation, right?

06:12.535 --> 06:14.953
Nah, I heard about it from Tsubaki.

06:15.132 --> 06:15.667
Huh?

06:15.840 --> 06:19.292
Kanji also thanked you guys.
Said you were a big help.

06:19.741 --> 06:21.261
I already said it, but...

06:21.864 --> 06:23.027
Thanks again.

06:24.246 --> 06:25.963
Please, I didn't do anything...

06:26.947 --> 06:28.036
It was nothing.

06:28.646 --> 06:30.141
U-Um...

06:30.578 --> 06:32.621
If you didn't want our side of things,

06:33.076 --> 06:36.892
then why, exactly, were we called here?

06:49.784 --> 06:51.132
Hey, Sakura.

06:53.606 --> 06:56.849
What did you think after meeting Endo?

06:59.255 --> 07:00.160
What did I think?

07:01.236 --> 07:02.633
He's a piece of shit.

07:04.301 --> 07:05.526
A piece of shit, huh?

07:05.889 --> 07:09.310
Tsubaki told me he took a shine to you!

07:11.335 --> 07:16.584
Well, that made me think it was
best you learned about him.

07:17.347 --> 07:21.803
And that means I'll also have to talk
about the formation of Bofurin itself.

07:22.849 --> 07:24.584
That's why I called everyone.

07:26.566 --> 07:28.763
I-Its formation?

07:29.138 --> 07:30.512
You mean how you guys enrolled and unified Furin,

07:30.513 --> 07:32.904
[Furin]
You mean how you guys enrolled and unified Furin,

07:33.353 --> 07:35.193
[Bofurin]
and then it became Bofurin?

07:35.784 --> 07:37.390
Do I have that right?

07:40.135 --> 07:42.283
Yeah, that's the gist of it.

07:43.495 --> 07:47.766
Right now, I'm going to tell you
about when we made Bofurin.

07:48.990 --> 07:50.406
And also about...

07:55.064 --> 07:56.440
the shadows left behind.

07:59.741 --> 08:00.326
Nirei.

08:01.224 --> 08:01.840
Yes?

08:01.981 --> 08:06.307
How familiar are you with the
details of Bofurin's creation?

08:17.538 --> 08:18.916
The time: Two years ago!

08:19.095 --> 08:20.375
April 7th!

08:20.904 --> 08:27.316
Five students of unified will enrolled into
famed delinquent school Furin!

08:28.830 --> 08:31.907
Then, warring factions vied
for leadership of Furin!

08:32.073 --> 08:35.483
Furin also did battle with rival
schools and external teams!

08:35.643 --> 08:38.972
It was the very picture of chaos, but!

08:39.920 --> 08:46.283
Upon enrolling, those five challenged
every one of Furin's factions!

08:46.430 --> 08:49.396
One by one, they brought them to their knees!

08:50.110 --> 08:52.855
Defeat, dispose! Defeat, dispose!

08:53.156 --> 08:56.756
With astounding alacrity, they
climbed to the top of Furin!

08:56.999 --> 09:02.470
[Thrashing]
Be the opponents second- or even
third-years, none could stop them!

09:03.070 --> 09:06.689
They converted defeated foes to
friends, growing their influence,

09:07.021 --> 09:09.716
and so conflict within Furin steadily decreased.

09:10.147 --> 09:12.264
Then, right when one year had passed,

09:12.775 --> 09:16.830
they finally achieved the hitherto
unheard-of unification of Furin!

09:17.932 --> 09:20.947
[Bofurin]
And then! Once they unified Furin,

09:21.366 --> 09:24.246
they became Bofurin, defenders of the town!

09:26.196 --> 09:29.218
And that... is the end of our tale.

09:32.381 --> 09:34.609
That felt like a rakugo performance!

09:34.726 --> 09:37.009
You're such an amazing speaker!

09:37.138 --> 09:39.396
Wanna perform on our stage?!

09:39.532 --> 09:40.412
Impressive.

09:41.513 --> 09:42.067
Th...

09:42.960 --> 09:44.516
Thank you.

09:44.775 --> 09:46.960
Man, thanks for that.

09:47.230 --> 09:50.995
Well, that feels pretty much right.

09:50.996 --> 09:51.483
Huh?!

09:52.996 --> 09:54.146
Hm? What is it?

09:54.147 --> 09:57.709
Don't play dumb! It wasn't that
simple and you know it!

09:57.710 --> 10:01.323
Now, now. You know Ume looks forward, not back.

10:01.716 --> 10:04.307
You're way too soft on him.

10:04.910 --> 10:07.446
Looks like I'm about to learn some things!

10:07.612 --> 10:10.658
Where'd all your nerves from before even go, Nire?

10:10.820 --> 10:16.400
Did you forget how we had to take thirty guys
on so you could fight the heads alone?!

10:16.658 --> 10:19.833
I got surrounded by scary upperclassmen a lot,

10:20.049 --> 10:23.126
but Ume always told me I did good after,

10:23.464 --> 10:24.615
so all is forgiven.

10:26.430 --> 10:27.315
Wow, really?

10:27.316 --> 10:28.603
You son of a...

10:28.695 --> 10:30.941
I mean, I am thankful!

10:31.901 --> 10:34.320
Now I can die without any regrets!

10:34.775 --> 10:36.695
He really does look forward!

10:38.596 --> 10:39.864
You exaggerate.

10:42.615 --> 10:44.744
Reform and suffering go hand-in-hand.

10:45.476 --> 10:48.246
You snapped every time your glasses broke.

10:48.596 --> 10:49.901
That was different.

10:50.295 --> 10:52.160
I'm with Ume on this.

10:52.726 --> 10:55.089
I only remember drawing a lot.

10:55.612 --> 10:58.283
You really did draw anywhere and everywhere.

10:59.384 --> 11:02.086
A lot happened, but hey! It was fun!

11:02.209 --> 11:04.116
You say that about everything.

11:04.418 --> 11:06.707
I know how Hiragi feels.

11:07.156 --> 11:09.046
It must have been quite a time.

11:09.864 --> 11:10.867
What gives?

11:11.600 --> 11:14.203
Where are the shadows in that story?

11:14.646 --> 11:16.295
Th-That'd be...

11:16.695 --> 11:18.910
Endo, wouldn't it.

11:20.369 --> 11:23.101
Well, yes, but...

11:23.286 --> 11:24.560
Wait, but?

11:25.409 --> 11:30.295
Next question, Nirei. How much
do you know about Endo?

11:32.529 --> 11:37.741
N-Nobody comes to Furin without knowing about him.

11:38.676 --> 11:39.858
He's a legend.

11:42.461 --> 11:44.793
Even I've heard about this guy.

11:45.323 --> 11:47.606
He was a first-year, just like you guys,

11:47.778 --> 11:50.135
but he made an ultra-violent faction,

11:50.498 --> 11:52.843
and nobody, of any year, could beat them.

11:53.741 --> 11:54.652
But...

11:55.390 --> 12:00.750
Where you guys built your forces
by befriending those you beat,

12:01.052 --> 12:02.516
they stayed an elite few.

12:03.070 --> 12:07.015
I hear they also went outside Furin
to crush other teams, too.

12:10.966 --> 12:13.563
Wherever Endo and his faction fought,

12:14.978 --> 12:19.329
it's said nothing was left,
as if it had burnt to the ground.

12:20.455 --> 12:25.753
They say that whoever caught
his eye was done for.

12:29.956 --> 12:35.667
And that meant he was the final and
greatest obstacle to Furin's unification.

12:36.486 --> 12:39.372
But still, the heroes defeated the legend!

12:40.572 --> 12:42.830
And thus Furin was unified.

12:43.618 --> 12:47.852
But Endo's faction wasn't like the others.

12:48.307 --> 12:50.960
They didn't join the unified Furin.

12:51.926 --> 12:53.643
They left it.

12:55.784 --> 12:58.504
Which makes them the shadows... right?

12:58.867 --> 13:01.390
Huh? Why does that make them shadows?

13:01.618 --> 13:06.775
I-I mean, they left instead of
unifying with Furin.

13:07.144 --> 13:10.849
That means they couldn't agree
with Umemiya's ideas.

13:11.550 --> 13:13.470
Their way of thinking was different,

13:13.796 --> 13:17.889
which means they might still view us
as enemies, and hold grudges.

13:18.116 --> 13:20.110
That makes them the shadows.

13:20.504 --> 13:23.144
The hell? That's just resentment.

13:23.600 --> 13:24.989
I thought it'd be deeper.

13:24.990 --> 13:25.593
Not quite.

13:26.923 --> 13:31.716
Nirei, there are two things you got wrong.

13:32.338 --> 13:33.113
First,

13:33.600 --> 13:36.935
they're not the types to be
motivated by resentment.

13:37.560 --> 13:39.932
That said, from what I've heard,

13:40.129 --> 13:43.815
Endo has in fact set his eyes on Furin again.

13:45.852 --> 13:47.144
W-Well...

13:47.624 --> 13:52.073
Wh-Whatever happens, you guys
have already beaten him once.

13:53.120 --> 13:53.956
So you...

13:54.633 --> 13:55.821
can do it...

13:57.058 --> 13:58.769
again, right...?

13:59.981 --> 14:01.901
That was your other mistake.

14:02.886 --> 14:05.864
They didn't reject our unified Furin.

14:07.181 --> 14:10.196
[Furin]
They cast Furin aside on their own.

14:11.372 --> 14:14.578
That was right before we hit the one-year mark.

14:15.550 --> 14:19.003
Furin was unified right at that
one-year mark, wasn't it?

14:19.316 --> 14:20.417
They left before...?

14:20.418 --> 14:20.996
Th...!

14:22.006 --> 14:24.541
That means...

14:26.270 --> 14:27.581
We...

14:29.052 --> 14:30.818
didn't beat them.

14:47.630 --> 14:50.492
Y-You didn't beat them?

14:51.286 --> 14:53.520
What happened, then?

14:56.412 --> 14:57.556
Well...

14:58.067 --> 15:03.507
As you know, we unified Furin,
made friends with everyone,

15:03.778 --> 15:06.270
and made protecting the town our goal.

15:07.796 --> 15:09.335
But Endo's faction?

15:12.547 --> 15:13.944
They liked the old Furin.

15:14.763 --> 15:19.200
They wanted chaos, a place with faction
warfare where might made right.

15:21.993 --> 15:24.363
We clashed with them countless times.

15:24.867 --> 15:26.603
We fought like hell every time,

15:28.123 --> 15:31.495
but never managed to settle anything.

15:32.541 --> 15:33.698
On the other hand,

15:33.827 --> 15:37.981
we kept fighting the other factions,
and thus growing our base.

15:38.756 --> 15:40.990
That started changing the vibe at Furin,

15:41.421 --> 15:43.255
and bringing it into order.

15:43.981 --> 15:44.849
Then,

15:45.316 --> 15:46.984
in apparently equal measures,

15:47.612 --> 15:50.800
Endo's faction lost interest in Furin,

15:51.107 --> 15:52.978
and they left it themselves.

15:54.030 --> 15:59.563
And they took all of the chaos and
brutality of the old Furin with them.

16:03.464 --> 16:04.615
And those...

16:05.058 --> 16:07.052
are the shadows you left behind?

16:11.569 --> 16:15.606
That's right. And those shadows are
once again approaching Furin.

16:16.418 --> 16:18.356
I don't know exactly why,

16:18.984 --> 16:20.480
but, worst-case scenario,

16:21.089 --> 16:24.750
they might be trying to return
Furin to how it used to be.

16:28.793 --> 16:31.021
B-But that's...

16:32.566 --> 16:33.913
Sounds good to me.

16:36.972 --> 16:40.430
If they come to us, it saves us time.

16:40.584 --> 16:41.772
Sakura?

16:42.080 --> 16:44.209
What, you scared?

16:48.160 --> 16:49.975
What we have to do is simple.

16:50.818 --> 16:54.756
It doesn't matter who comes at us.
We just knock 'em aside.

16:58.400 --> 17:01.175
Seriously... What a joke.

17:02.215 --> 17:05.347
I'm dumb as a brick. Fighting's all I know.

17:05.655 --> 17:08.670
What could be better than
fighting to be number one?

17:09.267 --> 17:12.424
Even though I once said that...

17:14.775 --> 17:19.415
People... Things... Feelings...

17:20.793 --> 17:23.113
You'll be able to become what you wanted.

17:24.203 --> 17:25.495
Until you're top dog!

17:25.889 --> 17:29.138
So I'm gonna work hard so you don't pass me by.

17:29.464 --> 17:32.141
Nice one, Sakura! Well said!

17:32.510 --> 17:34.209
That was satisfying.

17:34.307 --> 17:35.860
We like you a whole damn lot!

17:35.963 --> 17:38.160
You Furin boys are all like sons to me!

17:38.670 --> 17:39.729
Thank you.

17:43.316 --> 17:44.781
If it's important,

17:46.123 --> 17:47.243
you protect it!

17:49.015 --> 17:50.086
Isn't that...

17:51.938 --> 17:54.510
what being Bofurin's all about?!

18:02.258 --> 18:03.618
That Sakura guy...

18:05.390 --> 18:09.421
He said he came to this town because
he heard about the old Furin.

18:13.003 --> 18:15.470
Said it was perfect for him.

18:16.566 --> 18:18.800
But I don't think it is.

18:20.061 --> 18:21.052
I see.

18:22.720 --> 18:25.120
I hope we can be friends.

18:28.003 --> 18:29.880
Ahaha!

18:30.363 --> 18:32.307
Wh-Wh-Wh-What's your problem?!

18:32.492 --> 18:34.510
I said it because you were scared!

18:34.603 --> 18:35.261
Sakura.

18:37.033 --> 18:41.206
I really am so glad you came to this town.

18:48.080 --> 18:51.267
And that's why, if it comes down to it,

18:51.600 --> 18:52.886
I'll leave Endo to you.

18:57.803 --> 19:00.436
He's hardly ever taken an interest in anyone,

19:00.652 --> 19:02.916
but when he does, he goes hard at them.

19:03.563 --> 19:04.572
Be ready.

19:07.624 --> 19:08.972
Works for me.

19:10.855 --> 19:14.473
No complaining about me taking
your prey when I'm done.

19:14.898 --> 19:18.640
No worries there. After all,
he has no interest in me.

19:19.963 --> 19:24.547
Even when he was at Furin, we never
once had a direct confrontation.

19:24.972 --> 19:29.089
Hey, wait a sec, didn't you just say
you clashed all the time?

19:30.941 --> 19:32.123
Yeah, I did.

19:32.775 --> 19:34.203
With "them."

19:35.101 --> 19:36.972
There was another legend, you know.

19:37.470 --> 19:39.107
Huh? What now?

19:39.452 --> 19:41.292
I've never heard of another.

19:41.600 --> 19:43.938
I-I didn't know, either.

19:44.369 --> 19:49.175
But if they're a legend, does that mean
there's someone else like Endo?

19:49.956 --> 19:50.523
No.

19:51.581 --> 19:53.852
He's much stronger than Endo.

19:56.793 --> 19:59.206
The only man I never managed to beat.

20:02.406 --> 20:06.246
N-No way... But then...

20:07.846 --> 20:09.329
Who is he...?

20:13.532 --> 20:14.880
His name...

20:15.803 --> 20:17.212
is Takiishi Chika.

20:18.332 --> 20:22.024
And he was probably the strongest
man to ever attend Furin.

20:54.806 --> 20:55.378
Wha?!

20:57.876 --> 20:59.833
What happened here?

21:02.344 --> 21:04.092
Damn, Takiishi.

21:08.098 --> 21:10.067
I wanted to set off fireworks here,

21:10.584 --> 21:12.350
but they were here first.

21:14.898 --> 21:17.600
Okay, yeah. They were totally in the wrong.

21:19.009 --> 21:22.086
So, why d'you have them all piled up?

21:23.003 --> 21:26.024
Because it'll send the fireworks higher.

21:38.381 --> 21:40.381
Well, ain't that a flashy show.

21:43.649 --> 21:44.787
It's lacking.

21:46.006 --> 21:48.240
I thought they'd go higher.

21:50.049 --> 21:52.295
I'll need a bigger pile.

21:57.003 --> 22:00.006
[Strength for Another]

23:30.406 --> 23:34.510
Endo and Takiishi, huh? Doesn't
matter if he never beat you!

23:34.609 --> 23:35.556
Come get some!

23:35.649 --> 23:37.200
I'll send you all flying!

23:37.300 --> 23:38.583
You have us, after all.

23:38.584 --> 23:39.526
Th-That's right!

23:39.932 --> 23:42.209
This year's firsties are so reliable!

23:42.400 --> 23:44.443
I can't go losing, either!
